Where during the same period and under the laws of more than one Member State, benefits may be provided for the same family unit, the following priority rules apply: (a) if benefits are paid by more than one Member State on different grounds, the priority order shall be as follows: first, rights based on employment or self-employment status; second, rights arising from pension receipt; and finally, rights based on residence;  
(b) if benefits are paid by more than one Member State on the same basis, priority shall be determined by the following subsidiary criteria:  
(i) for rights based on employment or self-employment status: the country of residence of the children is considered, provided that such employment exists; additionally, where relevant, the highest amount of benefits covered by the conflicting laws will be taken into account.

